---
title: Breakfast Casserole for 11
tags: breakfast, casserole, eggs, sausage, make-ahead
cook time: 55 minutes
servings: 11
notes: Make the night before. Fills a 9x13 and an 8x8 pan. Pull from fridge 30 minutes before baking.
ai_image: true
---

The night before: Brown @bulk breakfast sausage{2%lbs} in a #large skillet{}, breaking it up. Drain fat and set aside.

Sauté @yellow onion{2%medium} (diced), @red bell pepper{1} (diced), and @jalapeño{3} (diced) in the same pan until soft, ~{5%minutes}. Add @garlic{3%cloves} (minced) and cook ~{1%minute} more.

Cube @day-old bread{10-12%cups} (french, sourdough, or sandwich bread) into 1-inch pieces. Divide between greased #9x13 baking dish{} and #8x8 baking dish{}.

Scatter sausage and veggie mixture evenly over bread in both pans.

Whisk together @eggs{21}, @whole milk{1.5%cups}, @mustard powder{1%tsp}, @Johnny's seasoning{} to taste, and @black pepper{} to taste. Pour evenly over both pans — bread should be mostly submerged.

Top with @shredded sharp cheddar{4%cups}. Cover with aluminum foil and refrigerate overnight.

In the morning, pull pans from fridge ~{30%minutes} before baking to take the chill off. Preheat oven to 350°F.

Bake covered for ~{30%minutes}, then uncover and bake another ~{20-25%minutes} until golden on top and center is set (not jiggly). Rest ~{10%minutes} before cutting.
